  "description": "Stripe operation wire-shape map \u2014 DATA consumed by do-work/stripe-request-mapper.mjs. Each row tells the generic mapper how one operation_id becomes an HTTP request shape: method, the vendor's published endpoint as a template ({provider_object_ref} substituted from input_facts[object_ref_key]), and which input-fact key carries the request subject, and optionally `acts_for_account` ({input_fact, header}): the header that makes the request act for the account named by that input fact. Each row carries the WHOLE address the vendor answers on rather than a fragment composed onto a base, because the vendor serves more than one versioned namespace and a shared prefix could only ever be right for some of them. Adding a Stripe operation = adding ONE row here ; the mapper enumerates nothing (L090 / enum-dissolution).",
